 "outcomeNote": "Ze'iri limits the baraita to unfermented wine.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "shabbat.139b.12",
   "daf": "139b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "גְּמָ׳ אָמַר זְעֵירִי: נוֹתֵן אָדָם יַיִן צָלוּל וּמַיִם צְלוּלִין לְתוֹךְ הַמְשַׁמֶּרֶת בְּשַׁבָּת וְאֵינוֹ חוֹשֵׁשׁ, אֲבָל עֲכוּרִין — לָא.",
   "en": "«GEMARA:» «Ze’iri said: A person may place clear wine and clear water into a strainer on Shabbat, and he need not be concerned» over the prohibition of selecting, as the wine is drinkable even without this filtering. «However,» doing so with «murky» liquids, «no,» one may not strain them."
  },
  {
   "id": "shabbat.139b.13",
   "daf": "139b",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "מֵיתִיבִי, רַבָּן שִׁמְעוֹן בֶּן גַּמְלִיאֵל אוֹמֵר: טוֹרֵד אָדָם חָבִית שֶׁל יַיִן יֵינָהּ וּשְׁמָרֶיהָ, וְנוֹתֵן לְתוֹךְ הַמְשַׁמֶּרֶת בַּשַּׁבָּת וְאֵינוֹ חוֹשֵׁשׁ! תַּרְגְּמַהּ זְעֵירִי: בֵּין הַגִּיתּוֹת שָׁנוּ.",
   "en": "The Gemara «raises an objection» from a baraita: «Rabban Shimon ben Gamliel says: A person may stir a barrel of wine,» mixing «its wine and its sediment, and place it in a strainer on Shabbat, and he need not be concerned.» Apparently, it is permitted to place even murky wine in a strainer. «Ze’iri explained that» baraita and resolved the difficulty: «That was taught» with regard to wine «between the presses,» when the wine has yet to ferment and will remain murky even after filtering."
  }
 ],
